  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f424be585f9e04c79a96c8292e8b9db1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dilema_AlgoritmoBeneficios
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: "Algoritmos em benef\xEDcios sociais"
  _titleEn: Algorithms in social benefits
  _category: 1
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "Modelos de risco aceleram a triagem de benef\xEDcios, mas aprendem padr\xF5es
    do passado e podem repetir injusti\xE7as. Sem auditoria, ningu\xE9m percebe quem
    est\xE1 sendo prejudicado."
  _summaryEn: Risk models speed up benefit screening, but they learn from past patterns
    and can repeat injustices. Without an audit, nobody notices who is being harmed.
  _realWorld: "Entre 2017 e 2021, Roterd\xE3 usou um modelo para pontuar cerca de
    30 mil benefici\xE1rios. Em 2023, a Lighthouse Reports mostrou que ele discriminava
    por etnia, idade, g\xEAnero e parentalidade."
  _realWorldEn: Between 2017 and 2021, Rotterdam used a model to score about 30,000
    welfare recipients. In 2023, Lighthouse Reports showed it discriminated by ethnicity,
    age, gender and parenthood.
  _tradeOffs: "Auditar custa dinheiro e exp\xF5e erros. N\xE3o auditar economiza
    agora e joga o risco em quem tem menos como se defender."
  _tradeOffsEn: Auditing costs money and exposes errors. Skipping it saves now and
    shifts the risk onto those least able to defend themselves.
  _sources:
  - Label: 'Lighthouse Reports: Suspicion Machines (2023)'
    Url: https://www.lighthousereports.com/investigation/suspicion-machines/
